# Feature contracts (`contracts/`)

When `@technical-architect` runs **`speckit-plan`**, it **MUST** create:

```text
docs/features/NNN-name/contracts/
├── database.md       # Feature persistence (tables, columns, indexes, FKs)
├── endpoints.md      # HTTP API contracts (method, path, auth, request/response)
└── permissions.md    # RBAC keys (view/modify) + admin menu gate
```

## Ownership

| Artifact | Owner | Phase |
|----------|-------|-------|
| `contracts/database.md` | `@technical-architect` | 3 — Design (`speckit-plan`) |
| `contracts/endpoints.md` | `@technical-architect` | 3 — Design (`speckit-plan`) |
| `contracts/permissions.md` | `@technical-architect` | 3 — Design (`speckit-plan`) |

Do **not** leave schema, API, or permission details only inside `plan.md`. `plan.md` may summarize and **link** to these files; the authoritative contract lives under `contracts/`.

## When to skip content (not the folder)

Always create the folder and all three files. If the feature has no BE persistence, no HTTP API, or no RBAC:

- `database.md` → state **N/A** with one-line reason (e.g. FE-only UI).
- `endpoints.md` → state **N/A** with one-line reason (e.g. no new `/api` routes).
- `permissions.md` → state **N/A** only when there is no admin API, no admin menu, and no `PermissionGuard` (see `feature-permissions.mdc`).

## Required contents

### `database.md`

- Tables/entities this feature owns or alters
- Columns with types, nullability, defaults, unique/PK
- Foreign keys and cascade rules
- Indexes needed for list/filter paths
- Migration note (new file name under `be/migrations/` when applicable)
- English only

### `endpoints.md`

- Method + full path under `/api` (and any public/product path rewrites)
- Auth (JWT, public, RBAC permission key)
- Request query/body (camelCase JSON field names)
- Success response shape (camelCase)
- Important error statuses (401/403/404/413/…)
- English only

### `permissions.md`

- Resource name and `{resource}:view` / `{resource}:modify` keys (or N/A)
- Admin menu href + required view permission (or None)
- Route ↔ permission map for BE middleware and FE guards
- Seed / `PermissionKeys` notes
- Template: `docs/templates/contracts/permissions.md`
- Rule: `.cursor/rules/feature-permissions.mdc`

## Consumers

- `@be` / `@fe` implement against `contracts/*` + `tasks.md` + `plan.md`
- Contract changes → update `contracts/*` (and note in `plan.md`); verify docs must reflect the final contract
- New admin features: BE must seed permissions; FE must gate **menu** and pages with those keys
